\details{
Each \verb{Array*} function returns a single array with named dimensions, while
corresponding \verb{ListArray*} functions return named lists indexed by stock.

Dimension conventions:
\itemize{
\item \code{Sim} — simulation index (\code{1:nSim})
\item \code{Stock} — stock names from OM metadata
\item \code{Age} — age classes
\item \code{Class} — selectivity classes defined by fleet selectivity
\item \code{Year} — model years, optionally restricted via \code{Years}
\item \code{Fleet} — fleet names from OM metadata
\item \code{Area} — spatial areas (\code{1:nAreas})
\item \code{MP} — management procedure identifiers
}

All arrays are initialized to a constant value supplied via \code{default}
and include fully named dimensions for downstream safety and clarity.

These functions are not exported and are intended for internal use when
constructing or populating operating model components.
